#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096459 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096672 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "739b1cbc-c1a7-547d-a9fb-1f244bd36827" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/id #uuid "b77c065c-3821-513c-9376-6e7108074616" :question/math-academy-id "e-4701" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n![](images/b3/b3512e604d6c4246c5582a75360076115c4bd9b6701c42587f318254b1c026a3.svg)\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n![](images/76/765eafb8a8b60aec9af512eeb666e2e13dbf83b8bc331b6effa75143930b4892.svg)\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=2$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+(2)=-2\\,⟹\\,y=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=-4$ and $z=2$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(-4)+(2)=1\\,⟹\\,x=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-5,$ $y=-4,$ and $z=2.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -5,-4,2 \\rangle.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096460 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096673 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd47a43f-1e99-5909-aa48-da8690025197" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination with Row Exchanges"}] :question/id #uuid "7760b6ce-91fb-5ba6-beb2-c244d6a73d69" :question/math-academy-id "e-4702" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n![](images/cd/cd75b39fc76773c0b3938ab6d60651e2b08dcd9ac325cc05718837934130ea07.svg)\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n![](images/93/933b897b7bc067610c87ea50a6fb871f04c5cc4610bd5bb0c868e6ffbac25e86.svg)\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get $a_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n![](images/42/42a1d61517661ccff31d9e603df548e79db7b0674a1f7f34c269a3a19e1c4bd6.svg)\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=1$ tells us the value of $z,$ and the second equation $y=3$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting these values into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+(3)+(1)=-2\\,⟹\\,x=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-6,$ $y=3,$ and $z=1.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -6,3,1 \\rangle.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096937 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096672 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "739b1cbc-c1a7-547d-a9fb-1f244bd36827" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2af7fa69-5175-5f82-abdc-7a83d1c7437a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,3,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414020} {:answer/id #uuid "3faa2fb1-77d5-521f-acea-30296fef736c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,1,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414021} {:answer/id #uuid "797daa95-425d-5598-93a6-9f8e22458433" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,2,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414024} {:answer/id #uuid "a48bd680-d71c-5a27-9b6b-4fee3480952d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,3,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414027} {:answer/id #uuid "c64960b9-232a-5479-96de-e63c3bb0d15f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,2,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414028}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a48bd680-d71c-5a27-9b6b-4fee3480952d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,3,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414027} :answer-field/id #uuid "145fd237-737e-5055-9883-501b0228a34c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414029}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6f82ff82-f58e-5dd1-b2bf-5cc0bd58f164" :question/math-academy-id "q-10676" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 13 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 & 25\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 13 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 & 25\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & -20\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 & 19 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+2z=19 \\\\  & y+2z=13 \\\\  & z=5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $z=5$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+2(5)=13\\,⟹\\,y=13-10=3.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting both $y=3$ and $z=5$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx+(3)+2(5)=19\\,⟹\\,x=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=6,y=3$, and $z=5.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨6,3,5⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097183 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096672 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "739b1cbc-c1a7-547d-a9fb-1f244bd36827" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "046f428e-556f-5956-b78b-d2844abad4b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284826} {:answer/id #uuid "babfedb6-0dfd-59fe-83fc-1aade7621c61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286487} {:answer/id #uuid "c1a979f3-bf84-5ce4-a382-9675dac8cb9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286562} {:answer/id #uuid "e3dfdeab-6885-5e75-a55d-ac0b26ea713b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -10 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286868} {:answer/id #uuid "f2ba7f8a-2143-5951-aadf-be80dd868963" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "babfedb6-0dfd-59fe-83fc-1aade7621c61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286487} :answer-field/id #uuid "78caa516-f3d8-59a7-8c65-740773cd1cf3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287404}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a19bbe50-faec-58bf-b57a-44ae8f766527" :question/math-academy-id "q-20505" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+2y+6z=5 \\\\  & y-10z=-11 \\\\  & 4x+8y+13z=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 13 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 13 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -11 & -11\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=-\\frac{1}{11}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -10 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368709 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096673 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd47a43f-1e99-5909-aa48-da8690025197" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination with Row Exchanges"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9341f62-c8f8-570d-80c8-63278f533fe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=13$, $y=4$, and $z=0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368711} {:answer/id #uuid "cf00639b-8c94-5353-94da-3f2b856bf365" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=13$, $y=6$, and $z=2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368712} {:answer/id #uuid "48282e37-d5c2-509a-8252-6ee2a8e03b3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-8$, $y=-3$, and $z=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368713} {:answer/id #uuid "3baa2212-ba77-51f2-be2f-5e043a5564f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=10$, $y=3$, and $z=-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368714} {:answer/id #uuid "da3d5251-f525-5757-9a3a-816f522e1513" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=16$, $y=5$, and $z=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48282e37-d5c2-509a-8252-6ee2a8e03b3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x=-8$, $y=-3$, and $z=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368713} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc8d2c28-de03-52ea-8fb5-2bfbbb958a9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368710}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3f809106-1e50-5a91-813a-0a376c6d5c21" :question/math-academy-id "q-73587" :question/problem "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." :question/worked-solution "Reducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -6 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -1 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-3y=1 \\\\ y-z=-4 \\\\ z=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=1$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(1)=-4\\,⟹\\,y=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=-3$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3(-3)=1\\,⟹\\,x=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-8$, $y=-3$, and $z=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414031 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096673 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cd47a43f-1e99-5909-aa48-da8690025197" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations Using Standard Gaussian Elimination with Row Exchanges"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1111935c-e645-5bcc-9a24-5310e4abf00c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414019} {:answer/id #uuid "48cbaac4-0396-5dd0-87a0-2f04eaf0760f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414022} {:answer/id #uuid "70ebcddf-aad2-5d94-849a-ae1ae9ab9ed7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414023} {:answer/id #uuid "8b765cfb-d1ea-559d-a6ff-8457bb546f81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414025} {:answer/id #uuid "979ac4ef-5db7-5cde-816c-7fb542951f8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414026}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70ebcddf-aad2-5d94-849a-ae1ae9ab9ed7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414023} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fa000c8-106a-5c36-ab34-ed3791f10731" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414030}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "db1a0a35-4ef3-5f5a-8985-ee685a957f6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-73593" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+6y-3z=-1 \\\\  & -2x-12y+8z=1 \\\\  & -x-5y+4z=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." :question/worked-solution "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -12 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -12 & 8 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply the $3$rd row by $\\frac{1}{2}$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
